{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far points to scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile as the best direction (0.715–0.725), but we lack a critical single-modality baseline: what does the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) achieve on its own with multiprofile and avgpool? Config_034 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool) directly isolates the image contribution using the same image encoder and aggregation as our best multimodal configs (e.g., config_049). If image-only approaches ~0.70, the RNA modality adds little and further multimodal tuning has limited upside; if it is substantially lower (e.g., ~0.55–0.60), RNA provides meaningful complementary signal and justifies continued multimodal exploration. This single experiment resolves the most important open design question—whether the multimodal fusion is genuinely additive or the image alone is near the ceiling—making it the highest-information-gain choice under a limited budget."
}

